*~
*.swp
*.cfg
*.tmp
*.img
workdir*

bin/
syz-cluster/bin/
dashboard/app/config_prod.go

# stub file used by Makefile
.descriptions

# coverage report created by make presubmit/test
.coverage.txt

# files generated by syz-sysgen
sys/gen/*
sys/register.go
executor/defs.h
executor/syscalls.h

# jetbrains goland
.idea

# vscode
.vscode

.gemini/
gha-creds-*.json
.agents/

# .claude per-user / per-machine working state (the shared docs under .claude/
# are tracked explicitly; see .claude/README.md)
.claude/users/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/tasks/*/local/
.claude/**/scratch/

# The fork's private area: embargoed findings, reproducers, maintainer
# correspondence, handovers. Never tracked; see .claude/README.md.
.claude/private/

# Private working records under .claude/tasks/ -- findings, reproducer steps,
# campaign logs -- must never reach the public fork. These were previously
# protected ONLY by .git/info/exclude, which is per-clone and does not travel:
# a fresh clone plus `git add -A` would have published them. Ignore everything
# here and re-admit the files that are deliberately public.
.claude/tasks/*
!.claude/tasks/README.md
!.claude/tasks/index.md
!.claude/tasks/mptcp_pm_selection/
.claude/tasks/mptcp_pm_selection/design_review_*

# Handover / evidence exports. These aggregate embargoed finding descriptions
# and funding material into one place, and neither the ignore rules above nor
# githooks/embargo_guard.sh covers them: the guard matches reproducer-shaped
# filenames, the private .claude paths and a content sentinel, and a numbered
# .md export carries none of the three. Verified: staging the directory and
# running githooks/pre-commit exits 0.
_handover_export/
